expected_issues.description:
Bug risk (operator precedence): `argv.yolo || false ? ...` is parsed as `argv.yolo || (false ? ... : ...)`, so when `argv.yolo` is truthy `approvalMode` becomes a boolean instead of an `ApprovalMode`. Use explicit boolean coercion/parentheses, e.g.:

```ts
const isYolo = Boolean(argv.yolo);
const approvalMode = isYolo ? ApprovalMode.YOLO : ApprovalMode.DEFAULT;
```

(and reuse `isYolo` for readability).

```suggestion
  const isYolo = Boolean(argv.yolo);
  const approvalMode = isYolo ? ApprovalMode.YOLO : ApprovalMode.DEFAULT;
```

